    "studentFacing": [
      "> What do you notice? What do you wonder? <img alt=\"Rectangle. 6 squares by 1 square. \" role=\"image\" src=\"https://cms-",
      "> Here are 3 rectangular prisms. 1 Caption: 1 2 Caption: 2 3 Caption: 3 These rectangles represent bases of the prisms. A Caption: A",
      "> Here is a base of a rectangular prism. Fill out the table for the volumes of rectangular prisms with this base and different heights. height multiplication expression to represent the volume volume 1 2 3 10 25",
      "> This is the base of a rectangular prism that has a height of 5 cubes. These are answers to questions about the prism. Read each answer and determine what question it is answering about the prism. 3 is the answer. What is the question? 5 is the answer. What is the question? \\(3\\times4=12\\) . The answer is 12. What is the question? \\(12\\times5=60\\) . The answer is 60 cubes. What is the question? 3 by 4 by 5 is the answer. What is the question?"
    ]
